# Runtime state, not repo content
_scripts/sync-check.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Commercially sensitive — only the .example template is staged here
estimation-data/rates.yaml

# Machine-specific paths (personal roots, exclusions) — only the .example is staged here.
# Article IX placement test: a file naming d:\WORK\AI\... is specific to this machine, not generic.
framework-data/scope.yaml

# Brand templates and the profile map that names them — organization property, not framework
# content, and the paths are machine-specific. Only the .example is staged here.
# sa-framework/ARTIFACT-SCHEMAS.md §8 records why this lives outside sa-framework/.
document-data/templates.yaml
document-data/templates/

# Client-specific render profiles — a named account's document preferences, and the fact that they
# are an account, are commercially identifying rather than framework content. Same reasoning as
# templates.yaml above. render-profiles/standard.yaml and client-example.yaml ARE staged: one is
# the framework default, the other the anonymised reference for writing a real one.
# sa-framework/RENDERING-CONTRACT.md §4 records the mechanism.
document-data/render-profiles/*.yaml
!document-data/render-profiles/standard.yaml
!document-data/render-profiles/client-example.yaml

# Builder test fixture — generated deterministically by tests/make_fixture.py, which IS staged.
# Committing both means the generator and its output can disagree, and the output is the copy
# people would then edit.
sa-framework/builders/tests/fixture/
